{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","prNumber":477,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/477","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:23:11.684Z"}
{"parentUuid":"68e158c0-55c9-49ae-b241-967689c36091","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14528964 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"656dcbca-84f0-46f8-94c1-3150b39c374e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:23:11.591Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14528964 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"656dcbca-84f0-46f8-94c1-3150b39c374e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNKNBthhrGy2wduJPDkV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mmhs4MzcWQL3K5iC75ufc9","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"Send brain half of merge handoff","message":"Brain half of the D4 handoff: 13 PRs, all Checks+Findings green, all now conflict-free against main, nothing still in flight.\n\nORDER (only two hard constraints, both ancestor stacks — the rest are independent):\n  #479 → #481   (479 is a literal git ancestor of 481)\n  #488 → #489   (488 is a literal git ancestor of 489)\n  #484 after graph #380 if you can; it degrades safely without it.\n\nTHE 13, one line each:\n  #473 fix(watch)    attribute every daemon log line            branch fix/distill-pipeline-v2\n  #474 fix(export)   one divergent cached transcript must not refuse the run\n  #476 perf(history) normalize the text once per call\n  #477 feat(doctor)  prove the MCP tool surface is reachable, not just declared\n  #478 perf(patterns) scope fact freshness per branch           branch perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint\n  #479 perf(export)  read routed checkpoint details concurrently\n  #480 fix(export)   say \"all\" in a way the host honours (it caps at 100)\n  #481 perf(export)  take checkpoint metadata from the local store\n  #482 fix(setup)    exempt every agent's hook config from the first-run gate\n  #483 fix(history)  one transcript too large to read must not refuse the index\n  #484 feat(brief)   carry graph's ancestor staleness\n  #488 fix(export)   an excluded session must not block the export\n  #489 fix(export)   a checkpoint whose commit no longer exists\n\nCONFLICT NOTES — two were genuinely conflicted when you asked; both are fixed and pushed:\n  #483 and #477 both collided with main's COR-2268 refactor (resolveLocalTargetRepoDir and the\n  read bounds / ReadBoundExceededError moved into internal/cli/internal/base and were exported;\n  the unqualified names no longer exist). Resolved toward each branch's own structure, adopting\n  main's names. Full prepush green on both, and re-proved by weakening rather than assumed.\n  #477's merge exposed a real gap worth knowing about, because it is a class: unwiring the check\n  from doctor left EVERY guard in its test file green — they all called the function directly, so\n  none observed the call site. Added a seam + TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck. I then\n  checked #482 for the same shape and it is covered (its install_ux_test.go guards go red).\n  Everything else: clean, behind by 2–19 commits, which the Entire gate treats as passing while\n  mergeable.\n\nCAVEAT ON MY CONFLICT SWEEP, worth building into your order: I verified each branch against main\nPAIRWISE, today. Six of them touch internal/cli/export.go (#474, #479, #480, #481, #488, #489), so\nmerging any one changes main for the next and the later ones will likely need re-resolution. A\nsimulated sequential merge is the only thing that would settle that — if your #381 integration PR\nalready combines the graph 12, the equivalent for these six is the thing still missing.\n\nFINDINGS — read this one carefully, I could not corroborate it. The Entire Gates \"Findings\"\nsub-gate reports \"passed — Agent review found no blocking issues\" on all 13. But I could NOT\nenumerate findings via the CLI to confirm it: every trail (org #384,385,387-395,399,400) answers\n`trail #N has no open change`, with --status any --freshness any --include-dismissed, with\n--project and with --branch. So there is no review change object to list against. Note the Partial\nGates summary on the same commits says \"Reviews don't start automatically on this repository, so\nstart the review manually\". I am reporting the gate's own statement, not an independent count, and\na passing Findings gate with no listable change is exactly the silent-zero shape that has bitten\nthis repo before. Do not quote \"0 findings\" for the brain half on my authority.\n\nOWNER: USER — nothing here is mine to do:\n  - Approvals on all 13. Suhaan said explicitly to leave the PRs open and stop asking, so I have\n    not requested review and will not.\n  - The transcript-mode decision (export.go all-or-nothing mode). Re-keying the distill cache\n    fingerprint means a paid corpus-wide re-distill, so it is his money. #483 downgraded this from\n    an outage to a quality/cost call, so it is no longer blocking.\n  - brain-store-delete: 37 GB, irreversible. Sequence written, held.\n  - graph #372, your lane, blocks code indexing on cli and entiredb.\n\nIN FLIGHT: nothing. Time your D2 fresh-env check whenever suits you — the brain build is final as\nof now unless a review comes back. One thing that affects your D2: devenv/ and cli/ had NO\nSubagentStart hook at all, which is why Explore/Plan subagents never saw the graph guidance (they\nnever load CLAUDE.md). Both are wired now. If your D2 measures subagent graph adoption, a run from\nbefore that is not comparable to one after.","type":"message","recipient":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Brain half of the D4 handoff: 13 PRs, all Checks+…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2873,"cache_read_input_tokens":194842,"output_tokens":1823,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1823,"cache_read_input_tokens":194842,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Mmhs4MzcWQL3K5iC75ufc9":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"Send brain half of merge handoff","message":"Brain half of the D4 handoff: 13 PRs, all Checks+Findings green, all now conflict-free against main, nothing still in flight.\n\nORDER (only two hard constraints, both ancestor stacks — the rest are independent):\n  #479 → #481   (479 is a literal git ancestor of 481)\n  #488 → #489   (488 is a literal git ancestor of 489)\n  #484 after graph #380 if you can; it degrades safely without it.\n\nTHE 13, one line each:\n  #473 fix(watch)    attribute every daemon log line            branch fix/distill-pipeline-v2\n  #474 fix(export)   one divergent cached transcript must not refuse the run\n  #476 perf(history) normalize the text once per call\n  #477 feat(doctor)  prove the MCP tool surface is reachable, not just declared\n  #478 perf(patterns) scope fact freshness per branch           branch perf/per-branch-fact-fingerprint\n  #479 perf(export)  read routed checkpoint details concurrently\n  #480 fix(export)   say \"all\" in a way the host honours (it caps at 100)\n  #481 perf(export)  take checkpoint metadata from the local store\n  #482 fix(setup)    exempt every agent's hook config from the first-run gate\n  #483 fix(history)  one transcript too large to read must not refuse the index\n  #484 feat(brief)   carry graph's ancestor staleness\n  #488 fix(export)   an excluded session must not block the export\n  #489 fix(export)   a checkpoint whose commit no longer exists\n\nCONFLICT NOTES — two were genuinely conflicted when you asked; both are fixed and pushed:\n  #483 and #477 both collided with main's COR-2268 refactor (resolveLocalTargetRepoDir and the\n  read bounds / ReadBoundExceededError moved into internal/cli/internal/base and were exported;\n  the unqualified names no longer exist). Resolved toward each branch's own structure, adopting\n  main's names. Full prepush green on both, and re-proved by weakening rather than assumed.\n  #477's merge exposed a real gap worth knowing about, because it is a class: unwiring the check\n  from doctor left EVERY guard in its test file green — they all called the function directly, so\n  none observed the call site. Added a seam + TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck. I then\n  checked #482 for the same shape and it is covered (its install_ux_test.go guards go red).\n  Everything else: clean, behind by 2–19 commits, which the Entire gate treats as passing while\n  mergeable.\n\nCAVEAT ON MY CONFLICT SWEEP, worth building into your order: I verified each branch against main\nPAIRWISE, today. Six of them touch internal/cli/export.go (#474, #479, #480, #481, #488, #489), so\nmerging any one changes main for the next and the later ones will likely need re-resolution. A\nsimulated sequential merge is the only thing that would settle that — if your #381 integration PR\nalready combines the graph 12, the equivalent for these six is the thing still missing.\n\nFINDINGS — read this one carefully, I could not corroborate it. The Entire Gates \"Findings\"\nsub-gate reports \"passed — Agent review found no blocking issues\" on all 13. But I could NOT\nenumerate findings via the CLI to confirm it: every trail (org #384,385,387-395,399,400) answers\n`trail #N has no open change`, with --status any --freshness any --include-dismissed, with\n--project and with --branch. So there is no review change object to list against. Note the Partial\nGates summary on the same commits says \"Reviews don't start automatically on this repository, so\nstart the review manually\". I am reporting the gate's own statement, not an independent count, and\na passing Findings gate with no listable change is exactly the silent-zero shape that has bitten\nthis repo before. Do not quote \"0 findings\" for the brain half on my authority.\n\nOWNER: USER — nothing here is mine to do:\n  - Approvals on all 13. Suhaan said explicitly to leave the PRs open and stop asking, so I have\n    not requested review and will not.\n  - The transcript-mode decision (export.go all-or-nothing mode). Re-keying the distill cache\n    fingerprint means a paid corpus-wide re-distill, so it is his money. #483 downgraded this from\n    an outage to a quality/cost call, so it is no longer blocking.\n  - brain-store-delete: 37 GB, irreversible. Sequence written, held.\n  - graph #372, your lane, blocks code indexing on cli and entiredb.\n\nIN FLIGHT: nothing. Time your D2 fresh-env check whenever suits you — the brain build is final as\nof now unless a review comes back. One thing that affects your D2: devenv/ and cli/ had NO\nSubagentStart hook at all, which is why Explore/Plan subagents never saw the graph guidance (they\nnever load CLAUDE.md). Both are wired now. If your D2 measures subagent graph adoption, a run from\nbefore that is not comparable to one after."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e61b057f-f45e-44a2-b6f6-bc77266c05f8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNKNBUu5K4ns2MiUeRVw","requestRef":"24f235c8-2400-4694-a14d-edf9d0c19b2a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"0295dee0-2e28-45db-9c67-d80fc4a3cb73","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:23:39.219Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
