ededError moved into internal/cli/internal/base and were exported;\n  the unqualified names no longer exist). Resolved toward each branch's own structure, adopting\n  main's names. Full prepush green on both, and re-proved by weakening rather than assumed.\n  #477's merge exposed a real gap worth knowing about, because it is a class: unwiring the check\n  from doctor left EVERY guard in its test file green — they all called the function directly, so\n  none observed the call site. Added a seam + TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck. I then\n  checked #482 for the same shape and it is covered (its install_ux_test.go guards go red).\n  Everything else: clean, behind by 2–19 commits, which the Entire gate treats as passing while\n  mergeable.\n\nCAVEAT ON MY CONFLICT SWEEP, worth building into your order: I verified each branch against main\nPAIRWISE, today. Six of them touch internal/cli/export.go (#474, #479, #480, #481, #488, #489), so\nmerging any one changes main for the next and the later ones will likely need re-resolution. A\nsimulated sequential merge is the only thing that would settle that — if your #381 integration PR\nalready combines the graph 12, the equivalent for these six is the thing still missing.\n\nFINDINGS — read this one carefully, I could not corroborate it. The Entire Gates \"Findings\"\nsub-gate reports \"passed — Agent review found no blocking issues\" on all 13. But I could NOT\nenumerate findings via the CLI to confirm it: every trail (org #384,385,387-395,399,400) answers\n`trail #N has no open change`, with --status any --freshness any --include-dismissed, with\n--project and with --branch. So there is no review change object to list against. Note the Partial\nGates summary on the same commits says \"Reviews don't start automatically on this repository, so\nstart the review manually\". I am reporting the gate's own statement, not an independent count, and\na passing Findings gate with no listable change is exactly the silent-zero shape that has bitten\nthis repo before. Do not quote \"0 findings\" for the brain half on my authority.\n\nOWNER: USER — nothing here is mine to do:\n  - Approvals on all 13. Suhaan said explicitly to leave the PRs open and stop asking, so I have\n    not requested review and will not.\n  - The transcript-mode decision (export.go all-or-nothing mode). Re-keying the distill cache\n    fingerprint means a paid corpus-wide re-distill, so it is his money. #483 downgraded this from\n    an outage to a quality/cost call, so it is no longer blocking.\n  - brain-store-delete: 37 GB, irreversible. Sequence written, held.\n  - graph #372, your lane, blocks code indexing on cli and entiredb.\n\nIN FLIGHT: nothing. Time your D2 fresh-env check whenever suits you — the brain build is final as\nof now unless a review comes back. One thing that affects your D2: devenv/ and cli/ had NO\nSubagentStart hook at all, which is why Explore/Plan subagents never saw the graph guidance (they\nnever load CLAUDE.md). Both are wired now. If your D2 measures subagent graph adoption, a run from\nbefore that is not comparable to one after."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
