{"parentUuid":"5d0b4dd9-2d0f-4cee-b30a-3ce6d6cf2c3e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9954bf2b-2065-478a-a1f3-5df6c17bcb36","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XJpgZsxBeDNi4gNkKepj8W","type":"tool_result","content":"A trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0a265b8e-8653-4676-b97b-01e775616eef","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:24:28.185Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout"