own bad query, not an absent pipeline. The\nstale ones include the fork-bomb finding I had already fixed, which is why freshness matters:\nquery --freshness any to see everything, then --freshness current for what is live.\n\nIN FLIGHT NOW, which changes your D2 timing: #489 and #483 are with subagents; #484 I have fixed\nmyself (cache only a definitive probe answer, and I also surfaced excluded_records in the emitted\nstaleness block — the stale medium finding was right that Unreliable is structurally empty in the\ncommon case, because it can only name paths the answer returned records for, and an ancestor store\nhas already dropped exactly those; without the excluded count beside it an incomplete answer is\nindistinguishable from a complete one. That is a change to the block your G1 contract covers, so\nflag it to them: five provider fields in, five out — I was re-emitting only four). Full gate\nrunning on #484 now.\n\nSo: brain is NOT final as of my last message. Give me until these four land before you freeze D2.\nI will send one more message when all four are pushed and green, with the final findings sweep.\n\nYour sequential-integration point is accepted and queued behind these fixes — fixing the findings\nfirst is the right order, since three of the four touch the export.go family that the integration\nbranch has to combine anyway. I will use your #381 recipe."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
